From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: Enforce a key's DACL when creating subkeys under it

S2 gate clause 3 (a non-admin cannot write HKLM\Software\Policies), and the
multi-user registry model generally. Wine checks a key's security descriptor
only when the key is opened; the recursive create path (create_key_object ->
create_named_object) never checked KEY_CREATE_SUB_KEY on the parent. So in a
shared prefix any user could create a subkey under an administrator-owned key
-- HKLM\Software\Policies among them -- because RegCreateKeyEx sends one
create_key request for the whole path and the server created each component
without an access check.

Two changes, both only in a system prefix and only when a thread is present
(server startup, which loads system.reg, has neither a token nor the intent):

  - When a new key is created, the creating token must hold KEY_CREATE_SUB_KEY
    on the immediate parent. A parent with no descriptor is allowed, so
    unprotected keys behave as before; a protected one (Local System and
    administrators full, users read -- patch 0002's default) refuses the write.

  - An administrator (the prefix owner, or root) may stamp that default
    descriptor onto an existing key that has none. Keys loaded from system.reg
    carry no descriptor, so a policy branch would otherwise stay unprotected
    even after sg-prefix-init "creates" it; now creating it as SYSTEM gives it
    one. Restricted to the SYSTEM account and to keys with no descriptor yet, so
    it cannot seize a key from another user.

Conformance (advapi32:registry) as the server's own account: 0 failures, no
regression. Measured in the shared prefix: a standard user creating under
HKLM\Software\Policies is refused (ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED), HKLM reads still work,
HKCU is still writable by its owner, and the SYSTEM account still writes both.
--- a/server/registry.c
+++ b/server/registry.c
@@ -753,6 +753,25 @@
             key->modif       = modif;
             list_init( &key->notify_list );
 
+            /* Stained Glass OS (S2 clause 3): enforce the parent's DACL on
+             * subkey creation. Wine checks access only when a key is opened;
+             * the recursive create path never checked KEY_CREATE_SUB_KEY on the
+             * parent, so any user could create a subkey under an
+             * administrator-owned key such as HKLM\Software\Policies. A
+             * parent with no descriptor is allowed (unprotected by design);
+             * startup and internal loads have no current thread. */
+            if (sg_system_prefix && current)
+            {
+                struct key *pk = get_parent( key );
+                unsigned int req = KEY_CREATE_SUB_KEY;
+                struct token *tok = current->token ? current->token : current->process->token;
+                if (pk && pk->obj.sd && !check_object_access( tok, &pk->obj, &req ))
+                {
+                    unlink_named_object( &key->obj );
+                    release_object( key );
+                    return NULL;   /* STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED already set */
+                }
+            }
             if (options & REG_OPTION_CREATE_LINK) key->flags |= KEY_SYMLINK;
             if (options & REG_OPTION_VOLATILE) key->flags |= KEY_VOLATILE;
             else if (parent && (get_parent( key )->flags & KEY_VOLATILE))
@@ -903,6 +922,24 @@
 
     if (get_error() == STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_EXISTS)
     {
+        /* Stained Glass OS: an administrator may stamp the standard descriptor
+         * onto an existing key that has none. Keys loaded from system.reg carry
+         * no descriptor, so a machine-policy branch such as HKLM\Software\
+         * Policies would otherwise stay unprotected even after sg-prefix-init
+         * "creates" it. Only the SYSTEM account (the prefix owner, or root) may
+         * do this, and only to a key that has no descriptor yet, so it cannot
+         * be used to seize a key from another user. */
+        if (sg_system_prefix && !sd && current && !key->obj.sd &&
+            (current->process->peer_uid == 0 ||
+             current->process->peer_uid == sg_system_prefix_uid) &&
+            current->process->token)
+        {
+            static const struct security_descriptor empty_sd;
+            set_sd_defaults_from_token( &key->obj, &empty_sd,
+                                        OWNER_SECURITY_INFORMATION | GROUP_SECURITY_INFORMATION |
+                                        DACL_SECURITY_INFORMATION,
+                                        current->process->token );
+        }
         if (key->flags & KEY_PREDEF) set_error( STATUS_PREDEFINED_HANDLE );
         if (!(access & KEY_WOW64_64KEY)) key = grab_wow6432node( key );
     }
